\begin{theorem}[Correctness of \Cref{alg:qNPMopt}]\label{thm:LearnProj}
    Let $\Pi\in\mathbb{C}^{d\times d}$ be an orthonormal projector of rank at most $q$, given via an $\bigOt{\frac{\eps\delta'}{dq}}$-approximate block-encoding $U_\Pi$. \Cref{alg:qNPMopt} outputs an isometry $W$ such that, with probability at least $1-\delta'$, $\|WW^\dagger-\Pi\|\leq \eps$, using $\bigOt{\frac{dq}{\eps}}$ controlled $U_\Pi$, $U_\Pi^\dagger$, two-qubit quantum gates, read-outs of a QRAM of size $\mathcal{\tilde{O}}(d)$, and $\bigOt{dq^2}$ classical computation. 
